**Finding (Correctness — Blocking):** Logical OR (`||`) treats `0` as falsy, so `input.qty = 0` is silently overwritten with `1`. Use nullish coalescing (`??`) so only `null` or `undefined` triggers the default.

**Scope & Checks:** Static inspection of the provided line only; no test runner was executed.

**Correction:**
```ts
const qty = input.qty ?? 1;
```

**Regression Test:**
```ts
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

const resolveQty = (input: { qty?: number | null }): number => input.qty ?? 1;

describe("resolveQty", () => {
  it("preserves zero and defaults only when nullish", () => {
    expect(resolveQty({ qty: 0 })).toBe(0);
    expect(resolveQty({ qty: 5 })).toBe(5);
    expect(resolveQty({ qty: undefined })).toBe(1);
    expect(resolveQty({ qty: null })).toBe(1);
  });
});
```
